tasks.prompt:
A marathon organizer has a JSON file with mixed registration records:

{"name":"Rosa","age":34,"category":"full","paid":true}
{"name":"Sam","age":17,"category":"half","paid":true}
{"name":"Tia","age":41,"category":"full","paid":false}
{"name":"Umar","age":29,"category":"relay","paid":true}
{"name":"Vera","age":16,"category":"half","paid":true}
{"name":"Will","age":52,"category":"full","paid":true}

Write a program that prints one line per runner identifying whether they are a minor (age under 18), whether they are paid up, and the category.

Output format (exactly these 7 lines, no trailing spaces):
Rosa: adult, paid, full
Sam: minor, paid, half
Tia: adult, unpaid, full
Umar: adult, paid, relay
Vera: minor, paid, half
Will: adult, paid, full
Minors: 2

The last line counts runners whose age field is less than 18.
